{"document":1,"title":"user in #5a4f22c0:answer_b0f3dfff_1: I'm trying to organize my contacts and reach out t...","updated_at":"2023-05-23T20:17:00+00:00","source_type":"slack","content":"I think this template is a good starting point. I'll start filling it out. By the way, I met Rachel, an old colleague from my previous company, at the TechConnect conference on February 10th and 11th. I should catch up with her soon. Do you think I should add a column for \"Company\" to track the companies my contacts are working at?\nAdding a \"Company\" column can be very useful, especially if you're looking to keep track of your professional network and potential business opportunities. It can also help you identify connections within the same industry or company. Here's an updated template with the added \"Company\" column: **Contact Tracker Spreadsheet** **Columns:** 1. **Name**: The name of the person you met 2. **Email**: Their email address 3. **Phone**: Their phone number (if applicable) 4. **Event**: The event where you met them (e.g. conference, networking meeting, party, etc.) 5. **Date**: The date of the event 6. **Company**: The company they work for (if applicable) 7. **Notes**: Any additional notes or reminders about your conversation or follow-up actions 8. **Follow-up Date**: A due date for following up with the person (e.g. to send a meeting invite or check in) Now, let's add Rachel to your spreadsheet: | Name | Email | Phone | Event | Date | Company | Notes | Follow-up Date | | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | | Rachel | rachel@example.com |  | TechConnect | 2023-02-10/11 | Old Company | Catch up and discuss new opportunities | 2023-02-20 | You can fill in the other columns as you have more information. Remember to keep your notes concise and focused on the key takeaways from your conversation. As you continue to fill out your spreadsheet, you might consider adding other columns or sections to track additional information, such as: * **Last Contacted**: The date you last reached out to the person * **Next Steps**: Specific actions you need to take or discuss with the person * **Tags**: Keywords or categories to help you filter or group your contacts (e.g.","metadata":"{\"Channel\": \"5a4f22c0:answer_b0f3dfff_1\"}"}
{"document":2,"title":"user in #5a4f22c0:answer_b0f3dfff_2: I'm looking for some advice on marketing strategie...","updated_at":"2023-05-26T20:59:00+00:00","source_type":"slack","content":"I'm looking for some advice on marketing strategies for my startup. I recently met Tom, a marketing expert, and he offered to provide feedback on my marketing strategy. Do you know any other resources or experts in the field that could help me? By the way, speaking of networking, I was just thinking about catching up with Rachel, an old colleague from my previous company, who's currently at TechCorp.","metadata":"{\"Channel\": \"5a4f22c0:answer_b0f3dfff_2\"}"}
{"document":2,"title":"user in #5a4f22c0:answer_b0f3dfff_2: I'm looking for some advice on marketing strategie...","updated_at":"2023-05-26T20:59:00+00:00","source_type":"slack","content":"Regarding catching up with Rachel, that's a great idea! Reconnecting with old colleagues can lead to valuable connections, advice, and potential collaborations. Make sure to prepare some specific questions or topics to discuss, such as your marketing strategy or challenges you're facing, to make the most of your conversation. Remember, networking is all about building relationships and providing value to others. Be open to learning from others, and don't be afraid to ask for help or feedback. Good luck with your startup's marketing efforts!","metadata":"{\"Channel\": \"5a4f22c0:answer_b0f3dfff_2\"}"}
